From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:58:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msm8996-common: stop extracting UnifiedSettingsApp

The Verizon unified settings app cannot start on this branch. It
registers a receiver without saying whether it is exported, which
Android 14 made mandatory, and the resulting SecurityException comes out
of Application.onCreate:

  Unable to create application com.lge.verizonsettings.UnifiedSettingsApplication
  Caused by: java.lang.SecurityException: One of RECEIVER_EXPORTED or
             RECEIVER_NOT_EXPORTED should be specified when a receiver is registered

It is restarted on a timer, so this is not one crash but a stream of
them -- 27 in a single captured log buffer, each with its own "keeps
stopping" notification. Nothing depends on the app; it is a Nougat-era
carrier settings panel for a carrier branch of a phone that is nine
years old.
---
 proprietary-files.txt | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/proprietary-files.txt b/proprietary-files.txt
index 0388cf31..0c67282e 100644
--- a/proprietary-files.txt
+++ b/proprietary-files.txt
@@ -585,7 +585,6 @@ system/etc/permissions/com.vzw.android.xml|19867261b1ac17dc7beea3514f86529a2ac5a
 system/etc/permissions/com.vzw.avs.xml|01e01429f9fab8de9b12eb941a17b8ad6b5b519e
 system/etc/permissions/com.vzw.vzwapnlib.xml|a9c540b9badabcd365759cb3052bb700b035638c
